# Images & Assets

**Path catalog:** `lib/core/constants/app_images.dart` (`AppImages`)
**SVG widget:** `lib/widgets/image/custom_svg.dart` (`CustomSvgIcon`)

There is no `ImageClass` wrapper. Use `AppImages` + Flutter/`CustomSvgIcon`/`Lottie` directly.

## Register assets on AppImages

```dart
// ❌ BAD
Image.asset('assets/images/logo.png')

// ✅ GOOD — add static on AppImages, then consume
static final String logo = pngImage('logo');
Image.asset(AppImages.logo, width: 94, height: 94, fit: BoxFit.contain);
```

Helpers on `AppImages`: `pngImage`, `svgImage`, `jpgImage`, `webpImage`, `jsonAnimation`.
Network base: `AppImages.baseUrlForImage` when building remote URLs.

Assets live under `assets/images/` (registered in `pubspec.yaml`). Keep Lottie JSON paths consistent with existing `jsonAnimation` usage.

## Display patterns

| Type | Widget |
|------|--------|
| PNG/JPG/WebP | `Image.asset(AppImages.xxx, …)` |
| SVG | `CustomSvgIcon(assetName: path, width:, height:, color:)` |
| Lottie | `Lottie.asset(AppImages.confeti, …)` |

```dart
CustomSvgIcon(
  assetName: AppImages.someSvg, // or path from AppImages helper
  width: 18,
  height: 18,
  color: AppColors.textSecondary,
);
```

## DRY rules

- Never hardcode `assets/images/...` strings in views
- New asset → file in `assets/images/` + named static on `AppImages`
- Do not invent a new asset class (`AppAssets`, `ImageClass`) — extend `AppImages`
- Prefer `CustomSvgIcon` for tinted SVG icons (e.g. text-field prefix/suffix)
